  "notes": "{待機|たいき} means standing by in a state of readiness, prepared to act when called upon. Unlike simple waiting (⟦{待|ま}つ→待つ：00469_matsu⟧), it implies alertness and preparedness.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {待機|たいき}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to stand by, to be on call\n- {待機|たいき}⟦{中|ちゅう}→〜中：09840_chuu⟧: on standby\n- {待機|たいき}⟦{時間|じかん}→時間：00468_jikan⟧: waiting time, standby time\n- {自宅|じたく}{待機|たいき}: staying home on standby\n- {待機|たいき}{児童|じどう}: children on waitlists for daycare\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{待|ま}つ→待つ：00469_matsu⟧: general waiting (neutral)\n- {待機|たいき}: standing by, ready to act (formal, prepared)\n- {待|ま}ち{受|う}ける: to wait in readiness for something expected\n\nREGISTER:\nFormal. Common in workplace, emergency, and military contexts. {待機|たいき}{児童|じどう} is a well-known social issue term referring to children unable to enter daycare due to lack of spaces.",
